# Zensim adaptive redistribution benchmark
# Date: 2026-03-08
# Encoder commit: a56aa5e (modified, uncommitted)
# Zensim commit: 499c811 (feat: add HF features to diffmap)
# Command: /tmp/final_benchmark.sh (4 modes × 20 images × 3 distances)
# Metrics: libjxl butteraugli_main + ssimulacra2 via djxl decode
#
# Config: K_ALPHA=0.15 (constant), L4 norm, no strategy splitting
#   DiffmapOptions: include_edge_mse=true, include_hf=true,
#                   masking_strength=4.0, sqrt=true
#   K_SPATIAL_WEIGHT=0.6, K_RATIO_MAX=3.0
#
# Modes:
#   e7       = effort 7, no iterative loop (baseline)
#   e8-bfly  = effort 8, butteraugli loop (2 iters)
#   e7-zen2  = effort 7, zensim loop (2 iters)
#   e8-zen2  = effort 8, butteraugli (2 iters) + zensim (2 iters)
#
# Dataset: 10 CLIC 2025 (1024×1024) + 10 CID22 (512×512), first 10 sorted
#
# Grand averages vs e7 baseline (ALL images):
#   e8-bfly:  size -4.24%  bfly -4.45%  ss2 -0.56
#   e7-zen2:  size +2.86%  bfly -2.34%  ss2 +0.91
#   e8-zen2:  size -4.20%  bfly -3.46%  ss2 -0.25
#
# CLIC-only averages vs e7 baseline:
#   e8-bfly:  size -2.58%  bfly -7.65%  ss2 -0.13
#   e7-zen2:  size +4.50%  bfly -1.84%  ss2 +1.18
#   e8-zen2:  size -2.51%  bfly -5.76%  ss2 +0.05
#
# Improvement vs previous benchmark (zensim_stacking_2026-03-07):
#   e7-zen2: size inflation reduced from +4.56% to +2.86% (ALL)
#   e8-zen2: now saves -4.20% size (was -2.92%) but SSIM2 worse (-0.25 vs -0.01)
#
# Key findings:
# - nosplit+masking+sqrt reduces e7-zen2 size inflation
# - e8-zen2 saves more size with this config
# - Separate 3-image test of 4 iterations (zen4) showed:
#   e7-zen4: +4.75% size, +1.65 SSIM2 (less inflation than zen2 on hard images)
#   e8-zen4: -2.85% size, +0.51 SSIM2 (Pareto-superior to e8-zen2 and e8-bfly)
